an  trade her soul for a chime of screams  which will make you scream with rage as  you cast at a startling rate of three  spells per minute last but not least is  the array of hidden doors hidden in the  old iron king DLC there are six in total  this first one is stupidly obvious and  gives you two soul vessels it's right  after the second dashing idol as if you  missed it the second is up on this  inaccessible shelf near the third ashen  Idol it's not really a hidden door it's  just a door that's hard to open you'll  notice that there are black barrels  blocking the door if you look at it from  this angle and it won't open until  they're smashed by hitting the door you  destroy the barrels through it and open  the door to kill this one enemy yeah all  that for one enemy who throws these fire  bombs that barely even hit you  the third is on the elevator that looks  like this  you spam the interact button as you ride  up it on the way to the hidden door and  you go through it on your way down  inside is the hollow skin headpiece  which makes you practically immune to  curse damage when worn  ah poor nashandra she just became even  easier the next three involve hurting  goofy barrel men to their deaths look  out for these brittle walls as you play  there's one here in this long corridor  containing a dispelling ring there's two  in the corridors surrounding the gated  area with black barrels one contains  Katarina gloves and leggings adding on  to the first part of the set found in  the sunken ground DLC and the last  hidden door contains eight count'em 8  petrified dragon bones which is pretty  awesome  so click here if you want to listen to  the story of this area but other than  that thank you so much for taking time  out of your day to watch this and I'll  see you next time
 

